  "live_records": {
    "q-76341": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76341",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $L=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the matrix $\\,L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{5}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{5}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\frac{1}{5}-\\lambda )-(-1)\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2} & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}\\lambda  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
