    "q-9348": {
      "dom_id": "step-q9348",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ -2+\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-3,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
