    "q-36780": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36780",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the matrix $P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(P-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-1\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ 49-7\\lambda -7\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +54 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-14)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 54 \\\\  & =196-216 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $P$ does not have real eigenvalues.",
