    "q-9339": {
      "dom_id": "step-q9339",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(B-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =1.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-9339-a",
              "type": "text",
